BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/History-of-Street-Skating-1.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://architecturehouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/05/History-of-Street-Skating-1.jpg
UID:OjmQfxuu8Bzx7CnfLZ0FN
SUMMARY:The Architectural History of Houston Street Skating
DTSTAMP:20260804T053532Z
DTSTART:20260926T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join lifelong skateboarder and architectural historian Ted Barr
	ow on a walking tour of the highlights of Houston’s Modernist and Late-Mod
	ernist architecture through a skateboarder’s perspective. The tour will co
	ver key plazas and buildings which became local\, state-wide\, and eventua
	lly global skateboarding destinations from the late 1980’s to today. \n\nA
	bout Ted Barrow \nTheodore (Ted) Barrow is an art historian\, writer\, cur
	ator\, and lecturer whose work bridges academic scholarship and contempora
	ry currents. Born in Bolinas\, California\, he holds a Ph.D. in art histor
	y from the Graduate Center\, CUNY\, where he explored the Florida painting
	s of Winslow Homer and John Singer Sargent through an ecocritical lens. Ba
	rrow has taught at Barnard College\, Baruch College\, City College of New 
	York\, and the University of San Francisco. Outside of art and academia\, 
	he is a distinctive voice in skateboarding culture\, known for This Old Le
	dge\, a video series that investigates the cultural and architectural sign
	ificance of global skate spots.” \n  \nThis program is in conjunction with
	 The Kinetics of Urban Movement\, on view at the Architecture Center Houst
	on from June 18-September 26. \n  \nExhibition Sponsors and Community Part
	ners \nKinetics of Urban Movement is funded in part by the City of Houston
	 through Houston Arts Alliance \n \nCherries Wheels\nHoney Skate Club\nHou
	ston Parks and Recreation Department\nHouston Skate Academy\nSelect\nSkate
	 ECOSYSTEMS\nSouthside Skatepark\n\nhttps://architecturehouston.org/event/
	the-architectural-history-of-houston-street-skating/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/the-architectural-history-of-hous
	ton-street-skating/
LOCATION:Tranquility Park\, 400 Rusk\, Houston\, Texas\, 77002
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ccs-houston.com/wp-
 content/uploads/2026/07/Banner-2.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ccs-houston.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07
 /Banner-2.png
UID:dvrlJejxeMgzXG1E8SpFW
SUMMARY:Nerd Yard Sale IV
DTSTAMP:20260804T053532Z
DTSTART:20260926T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:CCS Houston Nerd Yard Sale IV — Find Your Next Favorite Thing\n
	Your shelves are full. Your closet has boxes. Your collection has stories.
	 Now it’s time to pass them on. \nCCS Houston Nerd Yard Sale IV brings fan
	s\, collectors\, and hobbyists together for a weekend of digging through c
	ollections\, finding unexpected treasures\, and giving beloved items a new
	 home. \n  \n📅 September 26-27 | 10AM – 5PM\n📍 9700 Bissonnet St\, Unit 15
	00\, Houston\, TX\n🎟️ FREE Entry + FREE Parking \n  \n🔥 Event Highlights 🔥\
	n🧺 Sell From Your Collection\nGot boxes of collectibles collecting dust? D
	ownsizing your shelf? Ready to make room for something new? Set up a table
	 and turn your extras\, duplicates\, and forgotten favorites into someone 
	else’s next great find. Perfect for collectors\, families\, hobbyists\, an
	d anyone ready to clear some space while connecting with fellow fans. \n👉 
	Vendor Tables are open: https://tinyurl.com/CCSGuestVendorFromHouston \n  
	\n🔎 Dig Through Thousands of Fan Finds\nThe best finds are usually the one
	s you weren’t expecting. Explore tables filled with collections from every
	 corner of fandom\, including: \n📚 Comics\, manga & books\n🎮 Retro games &
	 consoles\n🧸 Plushies\, toys & collectibles\n✨ Anime figures & fandom merc
	handise\n📼 Vintage media & nostalgia finds\n👕 Clothing\, accessories & mem
	orabilia \n  \n🤝 A Community Sale Built By Fans\nNerd Yard Sale is about m
	ore than buying and selling. It’s about talking collections\, sharing memo
	ries\, and meeting people who love the same things you do. \n  \n🏨 Traveli
	ng to Houston?\nMake it a full weekend! Stay close to the event with our s
	pecial hotel rate for Nerd Yard Sale IV attendees. 👉 Book here \n  \nBring
	 your bags\, bring your curiosity\, and get ready to discover the next fav
	orite piece in your collection at CCS Houston Nerd Yard Sale IV.\n\nhttps:
	//ccs-houston.com/events/nerd-yard-sale-iv/\n\nFrom CCS Houston
URL:https://ccs-houston.com/events/nerd-yard-sale-iv/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ccs-houston
CATEGORIES:CCS Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT31H
END:VEVENT
